{
  "_doc": "Slice 4b (Task 1, the contract): the per-line rules for the list editors and the secret editor, shared by qbt (Task 2, tests/test_prefs.py) and the window (Task 3, SettingsView's node tests). Both must accept exactly the ok cases and refuse the rest with exactly the message given. cases: {kind, input, ok, normalised?, message?, why}. kind is the schema's listKind (ip for banned_IPs, trackerUrl for add_trackers, pattern for excluded_file_names) or secret (the three secretWritable keys, sent through `qbt pref-set <key> --stdin`). input is one line as typed (a secret as read from stdin, without a line ending). normalised is present only when ok: what qBittorrent 5.2.3 stores, i.e. input unchanged except ip, which goes through QHostAddress::toString (lowercase, compressed IPv6 per RFC 5952, IPv4-mapped kept dotted; tests/fixtures/server.py's _qt_address); compare IPs in that form. message is present only when not ok. why is a short note for a failed assertion's label. Rules: ip is qbt's announce_ip IPv4/IPv6 rule without the empty case, never trimmed. trackerUrl is http://, https:// or udp:// (case-sensitive) then printable ASCII with no | (qbt's valid_tracker_url without wss), at most 2048 characters; an empty input is a tier break (a blank line, shown as — next tier —). pattern is any non-empty text on one line, kept exactly. secret is non-empty, one line, no NUL, at most 1024 characters counted as code points, kept exactly (no trimming, backslashes literal). lists: {key, kind, input, normalised, why}: a whole newline-joined value as written to /app/setPreferences, and what 5.2.3 reads back. add_trackers is raw text (appcontroller.cpp:883, sessionimpl.cpp:3971): tier breaks, repeated blank lines and a trailing newline survive exactly. excluded_file_names is split on \\n keeping empty entries (appcontroller.cpp:670) and joined back, so it round-trips exactly. banned_IPs skips empty parts (appcontroller.cpp:783), drops invalid addresses, normalises through QHostAddress, sorts as strings and de-duplicates (sessionimpl.cpp:4167). An edit that doesn't touch a line must write it back unchanged.",
  "cases": [
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "203.0.113.5", "ok": true, "normalised": "203.0.113.5", "why": "IPv4 (a documentation range)" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "0.0.0.0", "ok": true, "normalised": "0.0.0.0", "why": "IPv4, the lowest octets" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "255.255.255.255", "ok": true, "normalised": "255.255.255.255", "why": "IPv4, the highest octets" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "2001:DB8::1", "ok": true, "normalised": "2001:db8::1", "why": "mixed-case IPv6 is lowercased" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "2001:0db8:0000:0000:0000:0000:0000:0001", "ok": true, "normalised": "2001:db8::1", "why": "full IPv6 is compressed (RFC 5952)" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "2001:db8:0:0:1:0:0:1", "ok": true, "normalised": "2001:db8::1:0:0:1", "why": "the first of two equal zero runs is compressed" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "2001:db8:0:1:1:1:1:1", "ok": true, "normalised": "2001:db8:0:1:1:1:1:1", "why": "a single zero group is never compressed" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "FE80::1", "ok": true, "normalised": "fe80::1", "why": "uppercase link-local IPv6" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "::FFFF:1.2.3.4", "ok": true, "normalised": "::ffff:1.2.3.4", "why": "IPv4-mapped IPv6 stays dotted, lowercased" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "::1", "ok": true, "normalised": "::1", "why": "IPv6 loopback" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "", "ok": false, "message": "Use an IPv4 or IPv6 address.", "why": "empty" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": " 203.0.113.5", "ok": false, "message": "Use an IPv4 or IPv6 address.", "why": "leading space: never trimmed, like announce_ip" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "203.0.113.5 ", "ok": false, "message": "Use an IPv4 or IPv6 address.", "why": "trailing space" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "127.1", "ok": false, "message": "Use an IPv4 or IPv6 address.", "why": "shorthand dotted form, not 4 octets" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "01.2.3.4", "ok": false, "message": "Use an IPv4 or IPv6 address.", "why": "leading-zero octet" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "256.1.1.1", "ok": false, "message": "Use an IPv4 or IPv6 address.", "why": "octet past 255" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "203.0.113.0/24", "ok": false, "message": "Use an IPv4 or IPv6 address.", "why": "a subnet, not an address" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "fe80::1%eth0", "ok": false, "message": "Use an IPv4 or IPv6 address.", "why": "IPv6 zone id" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "[::1]", "ok": false, "message": "Use an IPv4 or IPv6 address.", "why": "brackets" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "1:2:3:4:5:6:7:8:9", "ok": false, "message": "Use an IPv4 or IPv6 address.", "why": "nine IPv6 groups" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "tracker.example", "ok": false, "message": "Use an IPv4 or IPv6 address.", "why": "a host name" },
    { "kind": "ip", "input": "203.0.113.5\n198.51.100.7", "ok": false, "message": "Use an IPv4 or IPv6 address.", "why": "two addresses: add one line at a time" },

